{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["<b>Every article of work.</b> By this He informs us of the great abundance of the spoil of Midian, which alone was sixteen thousand and seven hundred and fifty. Further, He said <b>the men of the army plundered, every man for himself</b> — after the verse has already informed us above of the plundering by the men of the army, that they plundered for themselves; and moreover this is not the place for this information. Rather, it comes to inform us that not all the gold vessels of Midian were these, but rather what the officers of the army brought, besides what the men of the army plundered, each man for himself. And the intention in this is that they found for themselves great wealth."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:19.669955136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}